speedy is a multi-source fork: the engine is a fork of upstream SGLang with
selected patches from several community forks and own patches on top.
Every third-party commit keeps its original author in Git; the patch register
(docs/PATCHES.md, patches/register.yaml) lists each patch with its origin
(OWN, BACKPORT, BACKPORT-UNMERGED) and upstream PR number.

1. SGLang (https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang)
   Copyright SGLang contributors. Apache License 2.0.
   The engine is tag speedy-rc2 of https://github.com/thomasdenk79-cyber/sglang
   (a fork of sgl-project/sglang): SGLang nightly commit 25c1c439 plus
   backported upstream pull requests (authors preserved in Git) and own
   patches.

2. Pennyroyal / sglang-rtxpro6000 (https://github.com/jpezzulli/sglang-rtxpro6000)
   Copyright its contributors. Apache License 2.0.
   QSA serving work for the RTX PRO 6000. configs/adaptive-next-tiered.json
   is copied unchanged from Pennyroyal configs/pennyroyal/adaptive-next.json.

3. NVFP4 KV overlay (https://github.com/Lesilva/qwen38-flashnext-nvfp4-kv)
   Copyright 2026 Lesilva. Apache License 2.0.
   The NVFP4 KV cache for QSA is ported from this overlay onto upstream
   SGLang (see docs/PATCHES.md).

4. HyperBurst (https://github.com/aiueo52/sglang-rtxpro6000,
   https://github.com/aiueo52/hyperburst-rtxpro6000)
   Copyright aiueo52. Apache License 2.0.
   Benchmark reference. Ports of its draft MoE GEMV, MoE prune and PDL
   work are queued for rc3 (QFN-0193...0208 in docs/PATCHES.md).

5. NVIDIA pull requests to SGLang (#46153, #41624, #48249)
   Copyright their authors. Apache License 2.0.
   Backported while still open upstream; needed for the
   nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local checkpoint.

6. Draft token map (tokenmaps/hyudryu_top49152.{json,pt})
   From https://github.com/hyudryu/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-1xRTXPro6000
   (vLLM-based setup, token map version V3).
   Copyright (c) 2026 Mark (hyudryu). MIT License, full text in
   tokenmaps/hyudryu_LICENSE. The .pt file is the same id list re-saved with
   torch.save; the ids are unchanged. The dynamic draft-vocabulary ring
   (QFN-0099, QFN-0148) is an SGLang reimplementation and extension of the
   1K ring idea from the same vLLM V3 build, which also served the NVIDIA
   FP4-Local checkpoint first.

